      "writtenOn": "2024-02-21T11:24:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Q: What if we spawn a non-protected VM under protected ? Why don\u0027t we account for shared memory in this case ? Maybe we want to check if the system is running under protected mode ?",
      "revId": "55d6c2cbfdac44b38a606e25c4329014ccdf7dae",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c9a11005_ac61ee18",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hypercalls.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 386,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-21T11:27:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In that case, you can just check the entire vm footprint :-)\n\nThat\u0027s why it\u0027s called \"protected_shared\" It\u0027s like protected_but_shared. \n\nIt intends to make sure we don\u0027t leave things shared while they shouldn\u0027t.",
      "parentUuid": "fabcd511_fbf05e72",
      "revId": "55d6c2cbfdac44b38a606e25c4329014ccdf7dae",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e24c1676_af51e46b",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hypercalls.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 386,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-21T11:33:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As a user of this API I would expect to retrieve it in the same way for protectd/non-protected VMs without necessarily having a separate code path for non-protected.",
      "parentUuid": "c9a11005_ac61ee18",
      "revId": "55d6c2cbfdac44b38a606e25c4329014ccdf7dae",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "76e73e69_589c6cf5",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hypercalls.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 386,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-21T11:58:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s why it\u0027s called \"protected\", to emphasis it is for protected only. This memory that was protected initially and has been shared after. \n\nBy definition, that doesn\u0027t apply to non-protected VM.\n\nThe decision was due to the fact we have no other way of tracking this value, and it\u0027s been proved that it is important to keep an eye on it. While for non-protected VM, the shared memory is the entire footprint for the VM.\n\nBeside, I can\u0027t change this now, even though this is debugfs, as the behaviour is the same as Android14.",
      "parentUuid": "e24c1676_af51e46b",
      "revId": "55d6c2cbfdac44b38a606e25c4329014ccdf7dae",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a144efb_f3ffed81",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hypercalls.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 386,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942270
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-21T12:09:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I tend to disagree because I find it equally important to track the pages for non-protected as well. If you have to track a memory leak because you haven\u0027t given the page table pages back from the hypervisor, would you only test with protected vms ?\n\nThe behavior will be the same as on Android 14 for protected vm case and my suggestion is an extension to what you already do.",
      "parentUuid": "76e73e69_589c6cf5",
      "revId": "55d6c2cbfdac44b38a606e25c4329014ccdf7dae",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e730573_a015964e",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hypercalls.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 386,
      "author": {
        "id": 1951687
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-21T14:06:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is easy to track shared memory for the !protected VMs, the vmRSS gives you this and you would see problems there. So having this counter here does not bring anything interesting.\n\nThe definition for Android14 of this counter is \"memory that was protected but is now shared\". This is important, because we want to make sure we don\u0027t accidentally share too much memory. (or leave anything shared...)\n\nIf we would to account for all the memory of !protected VMs, we break this ABI in Android15. We change its meaning. Android14 expects this counter to be 0 for !protected vm.",
      "parentUuid": "6a144efb_f3ffed81",
      "revId": "55d6c2cbfdac44b38a606e25c4329014ccdf7dae",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
  ]
